{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe remote gate is refs/reconciler/gate. Older binaries require a non-empty gated_mode string and fail closed on unknown formats. Retiring the mode ladder therefore needs an additive, rollback-safe blob rather than a new-only schema. The writer retains gated_mode: reconcile-check while adding paused, reason, who, and paused_at. A vendored verbatim pre-change decoder must accept every new blob. Old mutating reconcile modes keep blocking on gated_mode; the read-only reconcile-check path remains allowed because __main__.py returns through _run_reconcile_check before check_phase_gate, and that ordering must remain unchanged.\n\nThere is no duration or automatic expiry. An --until field would diverge old and new readers and could silently unpause only part of a fleet, so it is explicitly out of scope. Pause remains active until an operator resumes it.\n\nThe existing set_gate and clear_gate ref writers already use expected-old-oid CAS. Pause and resume preserve that mechanism: a rejected CAS is surfaced as a clean conflict with the re-read remote state; it is never retried blindly or allowed to clobber another operator.\n\nPause provenance is deterministic. who reuses rebar._commands.identity._git_email(repo_root), the existing repository-scoped git config user.email resolver; its None result becomes a hard pause refusal rather than the identity subsystem's optional fallback behavior. Pause refuses without writing when the email is missing or blank and does not fall back to the OS user. paused_at is generated in UTC RFC3339 form only for the first successful pause. An idempotent same-reason re-pause preserves the stored who and paused_at exactly.\n\nA live error-path bug crosses the same seam: check_phase_gate runs before the reconciler try block today, so a corrupt gate escapes as a traceback. Move the mutating-mode gate read inside the protected path while preserving the earlier reconcile-check return. Corrupt state emits the exact stable line `ERROR: refs/reconciler/gate is corrupt; run 'rebar bridge resume' to clear it`, may follow it with the decoder detail, and returns clean exit 1. Do not rename check_phase_gate in this ticket.\n\n## Operator and workflow behavior\n\n- rebar bridge pause REASON requires a nonblank reason and writes the additive dual-format blob.\n- Pausing an already-paused bridge is idempotent only when the requested reason matches; it reports the existing pause without changing who or paused_at. A different reason refuses with the current remote state.\n- rebar bridge resume resolves only the observed ref oid and passes it to clear_gate; it never decodes or validates blob content before the delete CAS. It therefore clears a corrupt gate as well as a valid paused/legacy gate. Resuming an absent gate exits 0 with a notice.\n- Missing origin refuses loudly; CAS conflict exits nonzero with the re-read remote state; corrupt state exits 1 with the stable recovery line above.\n- A new paused gate blocks mutating reconciler modes as a benign exit 0 and emits exactly one stderr line: BRIDGE_PAUSED: {\"paused\":true,\"reason\":<JSON string>,\"who\":<JSON string>,\"paused_at\":<JSON string>}. Keys remain in that order; JSON string escaping makes delimiter characters and newlines unambiguous. Exit 0 is deliberate: the parent contract collapses new outcomes to 0/1/2 and explicitly classifies paused as benign 0, while every currently deployed workflow treats an unknown nonzero code as a red failure. A dedicated pause code would therefore break old workflow consumers and contradict the parent. The workflow distinguisher accepts only a complete line anchored at BRIDGE_PAUSED:, JSON-decodes its suffix, and requires the exact four-key set with paused=true; it never uses an unanchored substring match. This is distinct from both the existing legacy gated_mode-only throttle path and corrupt-state failures. This leaf does not rewrite the legacy gate exit mapping.\n- Pause and corrupt handling both short-circuit before pass-lock acquisition and run_pass, so neither may mutate the lock ref, tickets tree, or ticket ref. The real-repository oracle snapshots those states before invocation and proves they remain byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml preserves every existing rc mapping. The reconciler step gains an id and a paused output. On rc 0 it captures and replays reconciler output, sets paused=true and emits a GitHub notice only when the exact BRIDGE_PAUSED: marker is present, and otherwise retains the converged message. The commit-and-push step is explicitly conditioned on paused != true, so a paused run cannot deliver any state even though pause is exit 0. Nonzero corrupt and legacy gate outcomes still reach the generic error arm.\n\n## Dispatch and affected-surface inventory\n\nThe existing _BRIDGE_MODES mapping and launch_reconciler path remain the preview/sync mode-launcher only. _bridge_commands.py adds dedicated pause and resume subparser handlers instead of forcing them through that mapping: pause owns the positional REASON argument, reuses rebar._commands.identity._git_email for repository identity, and both handlers load the bundled _ref_lock module through rebar._engine.engine_dir, resolve the repository and configured sync remote, and call the new set_pause or existing clear_gate CAS seam directly. No child argument is forwarded to the reconciler and the legacy rebar reconcile parser gains no pause/resume write flag.\n\nThe additive ref implementation sites are _ref_lock.py encode/decode/read plus set_pause/clear_gate, _advisory_lock.py gate interpretation while preserving check_phase_gate, and __main__.py pre-lock branch/error mapping while preserving the reconcile-check early return. The CLI surface update also owns _bridge_commands.py parser/metavar/docstring, help/bridge.txt, help/overview.txt, docs/cli-reference.md regeneration, docs/user-guide.md, docs/exit-codes.md, and docs/release-notes.md. Existing closed-two-verb oracles in test_bridge_cli_heldout.py and test_gen_cli_reference.py are migrated to admit exactly preview, sync, pause, and resume; the compatibility oracle still rejects unknown future verbs.\n\n## Compatibility and test plan\n\nUse the parent epic's reader-first expand-contract ordering in two explicit phases. Phase 0 is already deployed: the pre-change decoder accepts unknown additive keys as long as gated_mode remains a real Mode member; the vendored verbatim decoder test proves that prior-binary property before any new writer is enabled. Phase 1 packages the new semantic reader and dual-format writer in the same binary, so an operator cannot invoke rebar bridge pause until the binary containing the new reader is deployed; no writer-only artifact exists. Feed every new blob to the Phase-0 decoder. Through the real bridge CLI and temporary git repositories, exercise first pause, blank reason, missing git email, already-paused same and different reasons, absent-gate resume, resume over a corrupt blob, missing remote, CAS conflict, corrupt reconciler read, and exact remote ref state. The corrupt-resume oracle plants invalid bytes, proves the ref is present, runs the advertised rebar bridge resume recovery command, observes exit 0, and proves the remote ref is absent without ever decoding the blob. Assert metadata stability and unrelated-state preservation. Exercise the old rebar reconcile --mode entrypoint against the new blob: mutating modes remain blocked for old readers, while reconcile-check still takes its pre-gate early return. For the workflow oracle, parse reconcile-bridge.yml, extract and execute the Run reconciler shell body with a stub rebar plus a temporary GITHUB_OUTPUT, and cover a valid full-line paused JSON marker, an unanchored marker substring, malformed JSON, ordinary rc 0, every existing benign rc, corrupt rc 1, and legacy gate rc 4. Assert only the valid anchored/decoded paused line writes paused=true and emits the notice. Separately parse the Commit reconciler events back and push step and assert its GitHub if expression is exactly steps.reconcile.outputs.paused != 'true'; actionlint/config-check supplies the workflow-syntax gate. Migrate generated/reference/help tests from the former exact {preview,sync} set to the new exact {preview,sync,pause,resume} set. No test asserts private implementation names or source layout; the closed-surface tests assert public help and dispatch behavior.\n\nSurface parity census:\n- CLI command: in scope through real rebar bridge pause/resume subprocess tests plus help/reference generation.\n- MCP or API tool: deferred to sibling f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d under the parent three-interface decision; this leaf does not preclude that parity, and persisted-format compatibility is tested at the shared ref seam.\n- Library facade: deferred to sibling f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d under the same parent decision; existing reconcile library behavior is unchanged here.\n- Automated callers: in scope through the scheduled workflow contract and real legacy reconcile entrypoint.\n- Dual direction: in scope; pause writes and blocks, resume clears and restores mutation, with exact remote state asserted.\n\nNo new contention harness is needed: each operator action is one existing expected-old-oid CAS operation, not a composed check-then-act outside that seam. The deterministic conflict test proves the operation does not retry or overwrite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every new gate blob carries paused, reason, who, paused_at and retains gated_mode: reconcile-check.\n- [ ] who is repository git user.email; missing identity refuses without a write; paused_at is first-pause UTC RFC3339 and same-reason re-pause preserves both fields exactly.\n- [ ] A vendored pre-change decoder accepts every blob the new writer emits, and real legacy reconcile coverage proves mutating modes stay blocked while reconcile-check preserves its pre-gate early return.\n- [ ] rebar bridge pause REASON and rebar bridge resume are the only new supported write path; old reconcile vocabulary and existing gate readers remain functional.\n- [ ] Blank reasons are rejected; same-reason re-pause is idempotent without metadata loss; different-reason re-pause refuses; resume while unpaused is a successful notice.\n- [ ] Existing expected-old-oid CAS protects pause/resume, and a conflict surfaces current remote state without blind retry or overwrite.\n- [ ] A genuine new pause blocks before lock acquisition or run_pass, performs no lock/ticket mutation, exits 0 with the exact single-line BRIDGE_PAUSED JSON marker contract, and causes the scheduled commit-and-push step to be skipped.\n- [ ] A real reconciler invocation against a corrupt remote gate blob exits 1, emits the exact stable recovery line, emits no traceback, and performs no lock or ticket mutation.\n- [ ] Following that recovery line with rebar bridge resume clears the corrupt remote ref by observed-oid CAS without decoding its blob and exits 0.\n- [ ] Existing legacy gated_mode-only exit behavior is unchanged and remains an error in the scheduled workflow.\n- [ ] Pause detects a missing remote and refuses rather than reporting local-only success.\n- [ ] The scheduled workflow notices only the BRIDGE_PAUSED: rc-0 outcome and preserves ordinary success, legacy benign, corrupt, and generic error mappings.\n- [ ] CLI help, generated reference, user guide, exit-code documentation, and release notes expose exactly the four staged bridge verbs while continuing to reject unknown future verbs.\n- [ ] No --until, automatic expiry, new-only blob value, check_phase_gate rename, or old-vocabulary removal ships."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786209214320154001,"uuid":"1672b457-a289-4339-9a1e-681cc4a80237"}